BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-30-bike_long-long-ride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270130T063000
DTEND:20270130T083000
SUMMARY:[RW] Long ride (120 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 100 min easy\; 10 min cool-down. Mostly stead
 y endurance (RPE 2-3\, 56-75 % of FTP if you use power). Eat and drink on
  rides over 90 minutes.\n\nWeek 10 (PEAK). Not medical advice\; pain that
  changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-30-brick_run-brick-run-straight-o@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270130T090000
DTEND:20270130T092000
SUMMARY:[RW] Brick run (straight off the bike) (20 min)
DESCRIPTION:20 min easy-steady run\, RPE 3-5. Legs often feel heavy for th
 e first 5 minutes: normal. Keep it easy: running straight after cycling c
 osts more energy than running fresh (Millet and Vleck 2000)\, and whether
  bricks improve that is unproven (Walsh 2019). Stop if anything hurts.\n\
 nWeek 10 (PEAK). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move mean
 s stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-31-run_long-long-run@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270131T063000
DTEND:20270131T074000
SUMMARY:[RW] Long run (70 min)
DESCRIPTION:5 min warm-up\; 60 min easy\; 5 min cool-down. Easy means RPE 
 2-3: you can talk in full sentences. Use your watch's easy heart-rate zon
 e if you have one.\n\nWeek 10 (PEAK). Not medical advice\; pain that chan
 ges how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-01-swim1-swim-technique-and-a@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270201T063000
DTEND:20270201T072000
SUMMARY:[RW] Swim: technique and aerobic (50 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min easy swim + kick\; 10 min drills (catch-up\, fingertip d
 rag\, sculling)\; 25 min steady aerobic\, RPE 3\; 5 min cool-down. Swim t
 ime and effort\, not distance: pools and paces differ. If you know your 1
 00 m time\, convert the minutes to metres. Rest 15-30 s between repeats.\
 n\nWeek 11 (PEAK). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move me
 ans stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-02-02-run1-race-effort-blocks-2@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270202T063000
DTEND:20270202T073000
SUMMARY:[RW] Race-effort blocks (2 x 13 min) (60 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 8 min easy\; 2 x (13 min tempo + 4 min easy)\
 ; 8 min cool-down. Settle into the effort you plan to hold on race day (R
 PE 5-6). Practise your fuelling here.\n\nWeek 11 (PEAK). Not medical advi
 ce\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
